IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bsma-types`

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — GOAL 3: THE MANAGEMENT CORPORATION.
--
--   "What does a subsidiary proprietor owe the management corporation, from
--    when does it bear interest, become an offence, and become a charge on the
--    lot that may be sold; what must the corporation keep, give, lodge and
--    insure, by when; and may the proprietor do this to the lot?"
--
-- Source: ../source/BSMA2004.txt — Part 5, Divisions 2, 4, 6-9 (ss 28-48,
-- 62-65, 69-88).

§ `Goal 3 — the management corporation`

§§ `Contributions (ss 40-41)`

-- s 40(2): contributions are payable "in shares proportional to the share
-- value of their respective lots". s 41(1): a proposed lot's contribution is,
-- while the building is being erected, "reduced by 75%"; (2) until a temporary
-- occupation permit is issued for any proposed lot in the building.
@ref ss 40(2), 41(1)-(2)
GIVEN total IS A NUMBER, `share value` IS A NUMBER, aggregate IS A NUMBER, `a proposed lot in a building without a TOP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lot's contribution, levy` total `, share value` `share value` `of` aggregate `, proposed lot without TOP:` `a proposed lot in a building without a TOP` MEANS
    IF `a proposed lot in a building without a TOP`
    THEN `the proportional share` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `the proportional share`
    WHERE
        `the proportional share` MEANS total TIMES `share value` DIVIDED BY aggregate

-- s 81: a subsidiary management corporation's expenses are shared "by the
-- formula A × C / B" — A the lot's share value, B the aggregate share value of
-- the lots entitled to the limited common property, C the total
-- contributions. s 83(2) and s 85(3)(b) apply the same formula to judgments.
@ref ss 81, 83(2), 85(3)
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 81 share, A` `A` `, B` `B` `, C` `C` MEANS `A` TIMES `C` DIVIDED BY `B`

-- s 40(6)(b): an unpaid contribution "bears interest ... from the expiry of 30
-- days after the date when the contribution becomes due and payable unless the
-- management corporation determines in a general meeting ... that any unpaid
-- contribution bears no interest".
@ref s 40(6)(b)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`interest runs on the contribution from` c MEANS
    IF c's `the corporation resolved it bears no interest` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `paid on`
         WHEN JUST p  THEN IF p AT MOST `the 30th day` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (`the 30th day` PLUS 1)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the 30th day` PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the 30th day` MEANS c's `due on` PLUS 30

-- s 40(9): if not paid "on or before the 30th day after it becomes due and
-- payable", the corporation may serve a written demand.
@ref s 40(9)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`a demand may be served from, for` c MEANS c's `due on` PLUS 31

-- s 40(10): a proprietor "who fails to pay any contribution or interest ...
-- before the 14th day after the date of service of any written demand" commits
-- an offence. FORK F3: payment on the 13th day after service is in time;
-- payment on or after the 14th day is not.
@ref s 40(10)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor commits the s 40(10) offence on` c `, as at` `as at` IF
    CONSIDER c's `demand served on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN
        CONSIDER c's `paid on`
        WHEN JUST p  THEN p AT LEAST (d PLUS 14)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `as at` AT LEAST (d PLUS 14)

-- s 43(1): an amount or contribution that "remains unpaid on the expiry of a
-- period of 30 days after the management corporation has served a written
-- demand" constitutes a charge on the lot once the instrument of charge is
-- lodged and registered.
@ref s 43(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation may lodge a charge for` c `, as at` `as at` IF
    CONSIDER c's `demand served on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d  THEN
            `as at` GREATER THAN (d PLUS 30)
        AND CONSIDER c's `paid on`
            WHEN JUST p  THEN p GREATER THAN (d PLUS 30)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 43(3): no sale under the charge unless "(a) a special resolution has been
-- passed ...; (b) a notice of the intended sale has been published once in one
-- or more daily newspapers ...; (c) during the period of 6 weeks after the date
-- of such publication, no payment has been received ...; and (d) there is no
-- legal action pending".
@ref s 43(3)
GIVEN s IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation may sell the charged lot,` s IF
        s's `a special resolution to sell`
    AND `six weeks have run since publication`
    AND NOT s's `paid in full after publication`
    AND NOT s's `legal action pending to restrain the sale`
    WHERE
        `six weeks have run since publication` MEANS
            CONSIDER s's `notice of sale published in an approved daily newspaper on`
            WHEN JUST p  THEN s's `as at` GREATER THAN (p PLUS 42)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 40(3)-(5): a new proprietor is jointly and severally liable for
-- contributions unpaid when it became proprietor; a mortgagee in possession for
-- periodic contributions, for others only if served with the levy.
@ref s 40(5)
GIVEN `periodic instalments` IS A BOOLEAN, `the levy notice was served on the mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a mortgagee in possession is jointly liable, periodic:` `periodic instalments` `, levy served on it:` `the levy notice was served on the mortgagee` IF
    `periodic instalments` OR `the levy notice was served on the mortgagee`

-- s 41(4): the Commissioner may approve additional contributions under (3)
-- "if and only if ... satisfied that the additional contribution is not
-- inadequate, excessive and unreasonable"; (5) after hearing the proprietor;
-- (3) only on (a) subdivision with extra expenditure, (b) an approved change of
-- use, or (c) a s 37 improvement.
@ref s 41(3)-(5)
GIVEN `a s 41(3)(a)-(c) ground` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Commissioner is satisfied it is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the proprietor was heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an additional contribution may be levied, ground:` `a s 41(3)(a)-(c) ground` `, reasonable:` `the Commissioner is satisfied it is reasonable` `, heard:` `the proprietor was heard` IF
    `a s 41(3)(a)-(c) ground` AND `the Commissioner is satisfied it is reasonable` AND `the proprietor was heard`

§§ `Funds, records and information (ss 38, 45-48)`

-- s 38(3): the management fund may be spent only on (a) s 39(1) liabilities,
-- (b) the corporation's functions, (c) transfers to the sinking fund, (d)
-- social and similar activities for all, (e) legal services; s 38(6): the
-- sinking fund only on (a) s 39(2) liabilities or (b) functions. s 38(9A):
-- neither on a collective sale except a general meeting under the Second
-- Schedule to the Land Titles (Strata) Act. s 34A(2): neither on installing a
-- fixed EV charger.
@ref ss 34A(2), 38(3), (6), (9A)
GIVEN `the sinking fund` IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A `Fund purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund may pay for, sinking fund:` `the sinking fund` `, purpose` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the corporation's powers and duties` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a s 39(1) liability` THEN NOT `the sinking fund`
    WHEN `a transfer to the sinking fund` THEN NOT `the sinking fund`
    WHEN `a social, cultural, educational or sports activity for all` THEN NOT `the sinking fund`
    WHEN `legal services for the corporation` THEN NOT `the sinking fund`
    WHEN `a s 39(2) liability` THEN `the sinking fund`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 45(3): the auditor is appointed at the AGM or by the council "not later
-- than the 90th day after the annual general meeting is concluded".
@ref s 45(3)
GIVEN `AGM concluded` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the council must appoint an auditor by, AGM concluded` `AGM concluded` MEANS `AGM concluded` PLUS 90

-- s 47(2): if no time is agreed "on or before the 7th day after the receipt of
-- the application", the corporation must fix a time between 9 a.m. and 6 p.m.
-- on a date "not later than the 21st day after the receipt".
@ref s 47(2)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the inspection must take place by, application received` received MEANS received PLUS 21

-- s 47A(1): a copy of an acquisition notice or award displayed "on or before
-- the 7th day after" receipt, "for not less than 14 days".
@ref s 47A(1)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`an acquisition notice must be displayed by, received` received MEANS received PLUS 7

-- s 48(1): records, keys and property must be delivered "not later than the
-- 7th day after service ... of notice of a resolution of the council".
@ref s 48(1)
GIVEN served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`records and keys must be delivered by, notice served` served MEANS served PLUS 7

-- s 48(2): records kept "for a period of not less than 5 years from the end
-- of the financial year in which the transactions ... are completed".
@ref s 48(2)
GIVEN `financial year ends` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`records must be kept until, financial year ended` `financial year ends` MEANS `add years` `financial year ends` 5

-- s 28(3): a change of address notified to the Registrar of Titles and the
-- Commissioner, and to each proprietor, "not later than the 7th day after
-- deciding". s 41(7): a comprehensive resolution under s 41(6) filed with the
-- Commissioner "not later than the 7th day after its passing".
@ref ss 28(3), 41(7)
GIVEN decided IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`notice must be given by, decided` decided MEANS decided PLUS 7

-- s 65(2): a transferor's notice of transfer "not later than the 10th day
-- after the date that the instrument of transfer is registered". s 65(8): a
-- reply to the corporation's notice "not later than the 14th day after".
@ref s 65(2)
GIVEN registered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the seller must notify the transfer by, registered` registered MEANS registered PLUS 10

§§ `By-laws (ss 32-33)`

-- s 32(4): a by-law or its amendment has "no force or effect until a copy ...
-- has been lodged with the Commissioner"; (5): it must be lodged "not later
-- than the 45th day after the passing of the resolution". (9): no by-law may
-- "(a) ... prohibit or restrict the devolution of a lot or a transfer, lease,
-- mortgage or other dealing ...; or (b) ... destroy or modify any easement".
-- (2): nor be inconsistent with a prescribed by-law.
@ref s 32(2), (4), (9)
GIVEN `lodged with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `restricts dealings or modifies an easement` IS A BOOLEAN, `inconsistent with a prescribed by-law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the by-law has effect, lodged:` `lodged with the Commissioner` `, restricts dealings or easements:` `restricts dealings or modifies an easement` `, inconsistent with prescribed by-laws:` `inconsistent with a prescribed by-law` IF
    `lodged with the Commissioner` AND (NOT `restricts dealings or modifies an easement`) AND NOT `inconsistent with a prescribed by-law`

@ref s 32(5)
GIVEN passed IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the by-law must be lodged by, resolution passed` passed MEANS passed PLUS 45

-- s 33(1): an exclusive use by-law needs "the written consent of the
-- subsidiary proprietor of the lot concerned". (2), (5): unless it says the
-- corporation keeps its s 29(1) duties at its own expense, the proprietor
-- bears them.
@ref s 33(2), (4)-(5)
GIVEN `the by-law keeps the duties with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor bears the maintenance duties of the exclusive-use area, kept by the corporation:` `the by-law keeps the duties with the corporation` IF
    NOT `the by-law keeps the duties with the corporation`

§§ `The lot and the common property (ss 2(9), 29-31, 37, 37A, 63)`

-- s 2(9): windows on an exterior wall "being either louvres, casement
-- windows, sliding windows or windows with any movable part, are part of the
-- lot ... and not common property"; all other exterior windows "are common
-- property, unless otherwise described in a strata title plan".
@ref s 2(9)
GIVEN `has a movable part` IS A BOOLEAN, `the strata title plan describes it otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exterior window is part of the lot, movable:` `has a movable part` `, plan says otherwise:` `the strata title plan describes it otherwise` IF
    `has a movable part` OR `the strata title plan describes it otherwise`

-- s 37(1)-(2): an improvement that "increases or is likely to increase the
-- floor area" needs authority by 90% resolution. s 37(3)-(4): one that "affects
-- the appearance of any building" needs the corporation's authority, which it
-- may give if it will not detract from appearance (or is in keeping) and will
-- not affect structural integrity — unless s 37A permits it (safety equipment).
@ref ss 37(1)-(4), 37A(1)
GIVEN i IS AN Improvement, `authorised by 90% resolution` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor may make the improvement` i `, 90% resolution:` `authorised by 90% resolution` `, corporation's authority:` `authorised by the corporation` IF
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `increasing floor area`        THEN `authorised by 90% resolution`
    WHEN `affecting appearance`         THEN `authorised by the corporation`
    WHEN `safety equipment under s 37A` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `neither`                      THEN TRUE

@ref s 37(4)
GIVEN `in keeping, or does not detract from appearance` IS A BOOLEAN, `does not affect structural integrity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation may authorise an appearance improvement, in keeping:` `in keeping, or does not detract from appearance` `, structurally sound:` `does not affect structural integrity` IF
    `in keeping, or does not detract from appearance` AND `does not affect structural integrity`

-- s 31(1)(e)-(f): the corporation may enter "(e) in the case of an emergency —
-- at any time; or (f) in any other case — at any reasonable time on notice".
@ref s 31(1)
GIVEN emergency IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `notice given to the occupier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation may enter the lot, emergency:` emergency `, reasonable time:` `a reasonable time` `, notice:` `notice given to the occupier` IF
    emergency OR (`a reasonable time` AND `notice given to the occupier`)

-- s 30(5): the corporation "must carry out" work to rectify a structural defect
-- affecting support or shelter, or a defect in a s 63(a)(ii) service pipe,
-- where the defect "is not due to any breach of the duty imposed ... by
-- section 63(a)"; it may recover the cost from the person with a duty to
-- remedy it.
@ref s 30(5)
GIVEN `a structural or service-pipe defect within the lot` IS A BOOLEAN, `due to a breach of s 63(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation must rectify the defect, defect:` `a structural or service-pipe defect within the lot` `, due to a s 63(a) breach:` `due to a breach of s 63(a)` IF
    `a structural or service-pipe defect within the lot` AND NOT `due to a breach of s 63(a)`

§§ `Insurance (ss 70-73)`

-- s 70(1): "Unless otherwise directed by a resolution by consensus", the
-- corporation must insure every subdivided building under a damage policy.
@ref s 70(1)
GIVEN `a resolution by consensus directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation must keep a damage policy, consensus otherwise:` `a resolution by consensus directs otherwise` IF
    NOT `a resolution by consensus directs otherwise`

-- s 73(1)(a)(ii): the insurer of a mortgaged lot pays "the amount stated in the
-- contract, the amount of the loss, or an amount sufficient ... to discharge
-- mortgages ..., whichever is the least amount".
@ref s 73(1)(a)(ii)
GIVEN insured IS A NUMBER, loss IS A NUMBER, `to discharge the mortgages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the mortgaged-lot insurer pays, insured` insured `, loss` loss `, to discharge` `to discharge the mortgages` MEANS
    `the least` insured (`the least` loss `to discharge the mortgages`)
    WHERE
        `the least` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 24, 28(1)-(2), 29, 30(1)-(4), (6), 32(1)-(3A), (6)-(12), 33(1), (3), (6)-(7), 34-36, 38(1)-(2), (4)-(10), 39, 40(1), (7), (11)-(12), 41(9), 42, 43(2), (4)-(10), 44, 45(1)-(2), 46, 47(1), (1A), (3)-(4), 62-64, 65(1), (3)-(12), 69, 71, 72, 74-80, 82-88
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`corporation provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 29: the corporation's duties to control, maintain, renew, insure, comply with notices, keep records and convene AGMs; fixed EV chargers; limited common property"
         "s 30(1)-(4), (6): the corporation's power to do work a proprietor fails to do, and recover the cost as a debt"
         "ss 32-33: by-law purposes, binding effect, records, copies, court enforcement; exclusive use terms and transposition"
         "ss 34-36: transfers, leases, additional common property, amalgamation, easements (resolutions in Goal 1); court orders where a meeting is impracticable"
         "ss 38-39: what each fund receives; investment as trust funds; bank account; borrowing; return of funds on collective sale; books and statements; what contributions are for"
         "ss 40(1), (7), (11)-(12), 42, 43(2), (4)-(10), 44: levy by notice; interest to the fund; court order to pay; contributions before the first AGM; the charge's priority, registration and discharge; members' guarantee"
         "ss 45(1)-(2), 46, 47: audit by a public accountant; the strata roll; information and certificates on application"
         "ss 62-65: share values; proprietors' duties not to interfere with support, services or others' enjoyment; company representatives; notices by proprietors and mortgagees"
         "ss 69, 71, 72, 74, 75: insurance definitions, further insurance by ordinary resolution, proprietors' own insurance, rebuilding, insurable interest"
         "ss 76-84: subsidiary management corporations and limited common property — application, purposes, designation, functions, executive committee, by-laws, judgments, termination"
         "ss 85-88: representation in proceedings, non-lot acquisition, structural-defect proceedings as agent, costs, court orders for breach"
